# Architecture — ai-client

Created: 2026-11-05.

A local web application for the developer's own Linux machine. One browser page manages several interactive Claude Code CLI sessions. The backend spawns processes in pseudo-terminals and streams them to the browser over WebSocket. The frontend renders the terminals.

## Stack

| Item | Choice |
|------|--------|
| Language | TypeScript 7.0 (`strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`) |
| Runtime | Node.js 22 (installed v22.23.4), Linux only |
| Package manager | npm 10.9.9, single package, no workspaces, ESM (`"type": "module"`) |
| Backend | Fastify 5 + @fastify/websocket + @fastify/static, node-pty, run with `tsx` |
| Frontend | React 18 + Vite 8, @xterm/xterm 6 + @xterm/addon-fit, plain CSS |
| Desktop | Electron 45 main process, compiled by `tsc` to `dist/desktop` |
| Tests | Vitest 5 (unit/integration), Playwright 1.64 with chromium (e2e) |

## Structure

```
.
├── package.json / package-lock.json
├── tsconfig.json            solution file: references the three configs below
├── tsconfig.server.json     src/server (NodeNext resolution, Node types)
├── tsconfig.web.json        src/web (bundler resolution, DOM, react-jsx)
├── tsconfig.node.json       root config files (vite, vitest, playwright)
├── tsconfig.desktop.json    src/desktop (NodeNext resolution, Node and Electron types)
├── tsconfig.desktop.build.json  emits src/desktop to dist/desktop, without the tests
├── vite.config.ts           root src/web, output dist/web, dev proxy /api -> server
├── vitest.config.ts         tests in src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}
├── playwright.config.ts     tests in e2e/, builds and starts the app on port 3100
├── .gitignore
└── src/
    ├── server/main.ts       Fastify app: GET /api/health, serves dist/web if it exists
    ├── web/
    │   ├── index.html       Vite entry page
    │   └── main.tsx         React root, renders a placeholder title
    └── desktop/
        ├── main.ts          Electron main process (package.json "main" points to its build)
        ├── desktop-bridge.cts  preload of the window, emitted as CommonJS (`dist/desktop/desktop-bridge.cjs`)
        └── icons/           app icon, SVG and 256 px PNG
```

Generated output, not versioned: `dist/web/` (frontend build), `dist/desktop/` (desktop build), `test-results/`, `playwright-report/`.

## Dependencies

| Package | Kind | Why |
|---------|------|-----|
| fastify | runtime | HTTP server |
| @fastify/websocket | runtime | WebSocket transport for terminal streams |
| @fastify/static | runtime | Serves the built frontend from `dist/web` |
| node-pty | runtime | Pseudo-terminals for the CLI sessions (native build) |
| tsx | runtime | Runs the TypeScript server in `dev` and `start` |
| electron | runtime | Desktop window; the app runs it from the repository |
| react, react-dom | runtime | UI |
| @xterm/xterm, @xterm/addon-fit | runtime | Terminal view and resize to container |
| @xterm/headless, @xterm/addon-serialize | runtime | Server-side terminal mirror per session and its serialized snapshot |
| @jellybrick/dbus-next | runtime | D-Bus client of the desktop app for the system notifications (assumption "Notification mechanism"). Pure JavaScript, no native build |
| typescript | dev | Typecheck (`tsc -b`, no emit) |
| vite, @vitejs/plugin-react | dev | Frontend dev server and bundle |
| vitest | dev | Unit and integration tests |
| @playwright/test | dev | e2e tests in chromium |
| concurrently | dev | Runs server and Vite together in `dev` |
| @types/node, @types/react, @types/react-dom, @types/ws | dev | Type definitions |

## Conventions

- Backend code lives in `src/server/`, frontend code in `src/web/`. They do not import each other.
- Desktop code lives in `src/desktop/`. It imports neither `src/server` nor `src/web`. It starts the server as a separate process with the system Node and loads the page over HTTP.
- Desktop imports use the `.js` extension, as in the server.
- The window preload is a `.cts` file. `tsc` emits it as CommonJS, because Electron runs a sandboxed preload as a script. It can `require` only `electron`, so it imports no local module.
- Server imports use the `.js` extension (NodeNext ESM resolution).
- File names are kebab-case. React component files are PascalCase (`SessionList.tsx`).
- Unit tests sit next to the code: `<name>.test.ts` / `<name>.test.tsx`.
- e2e tests go in `e2e/*.spec.ts`. The folder does not exist yet.
- HTTP and WebSocket routes use the `/api` prefix. The dev proxy forwards only `/api`.
- The server binds to `127.0.0.1` only. Port comes from `PORT` (default 3000).

## Commands

| Goal | Command | Quiet variant (for agents) |
|------|---------|----------------------------|
| Install | `npm install` | `npm install --silent` |
| Dev (server :3000 + Vite :5173) | `npm run dev` | — |
| Typecheck only | `npx tsc -b` | same (silent on success) |
| Build | `npm run build` | `npx tsc -b && npx vite build --logLevel warn` |
| Start built app (:4001) | `npm start` | `npm run --silent start` |
| Build the desktop app | `npm run build:desktop` | `npm run --silent build:desktop` |
| Launch the desktop app | `npm run desktop` | — |
| Install the menu entry | `npm run desktop:install` | — |
| Unit tests | `npm test` | `npx vitest run --reporter=dot` |
| One unit test file | `npx vitest run <path>` | `npx vitest run --reporter=dot <path>` |
| e2e tests (browser only, never Electron) | `npm run test:e2e` | `npx playwright test --pass-with-no-tests --reporter=dot` |
| One e2e file | `npx playwright test <path>` | `npx playwright test --reporter=dot <path>` |
| e2e desktop (Electron, opens windows on the display, 1 worker) | `npm run test:e2e:desktop` | `E2E_DESKTOP=1 npx playwright test --reporter=dot` |
| Install e2e browser | `npx playwright install chromium` | — |

The e2e run builds the app and starts it on port 3100. A server already listening there is reused outside CI.

## Assumptions

- **TypeScript 7.** npm resolved the latest major (7.0.2). Build mode (`tsc -b`) and the configs work with it.
- **No server compile step.** `start` runs `src/server/main.ts` with `tsx`, so `tsx` is a runtime dependency. The app is local and always runs from the repository.
- **Separate dev servers.** In `dev`, Vite serves the page and proxies `/api` (HTTP and WebSocket) to Fastify. The server registers static files only when `dist/web` exists.
- **Ports.** 3000 for the server, 5173 for Vite (`strictPort`), 3100 for e2e. A separate e2e port avoids a clash with a running instance.
- **Empty test runs pass.** Vitest uses `passWithNoTests`. `test:e2e` passes `--pass-with-no-tests`.
- **No jsdom.** Vitest runs in the Node environment. A DOM environment is added when the first component test needs it.
- **GUI language.** English, as the analysis `claude_sessions_client-ui_redesign-material3_mock-studio_dark-english_ui` sets. Code identifiers stay in English.
- **No linter or formatter.** Not requested.
- **Playwright browser.** Chromium headless shell installed (v1248) in `~/.cache/ms-playwright`.
- **node-pty.** Version 1.1.0 installs and loads on Node 22 in this machine.
- **Electron sandbox.** Ubuntu 24.04 AppArmor (`kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns = 1`) blocks the Chromium sandbox of an Electron run from `node_modules`: launched from the menu it aborts ("SUID sandbox helper … not configured correctly"). The menu entry and `npm run desktop` pass `--no-sandbox` (human decision, 2026-11-06). A shell inside the IntelliJ snap hides the problem: its AppArmor profile is in complain mode.
- **Notification mechanism.** The desktop app talks to `org.freedesktop.Notifications` over the D-Bus session bus: `Notify` with `replaces_id`, `CloseNotification`, and the signals `ActionInvoked` and `NotificationClosed`. Electron's `Notification` cannot replace a notification in place on Linux: `show()` closes it and creates a new one, and Electron 45 does not load `notify_notification_update`. Checked on 2026-11-06.
- **Desktop port.** The desktop app looks for the backend on `PORT`, default 4001, the port of `npm start`. It starts the server on that port when none answers. Gatekeeper decision, 2026-11-06.
- **Node for the desktop app.** The desktop session has no nvm `PATH`. The menu entry passes the absolute Node path in `AI_CLIENT_NODE`. `npm run desktop` uses `node` from the shell.
- **Menu entry folder.** `npm run desktop:install` writes to `AI_CLIENT_APPLICATIONS_DIR` when set, else to `$XDG_DATA_HOME/applications` (default `~/.local/share/applications`).
- **`NODE_ENV=production` in the shell** makes npm skip dev dependencies. Install with `npm install --include=dev`.
